    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We note that the projection $S \rightarrow \ast $, being a composition of left fibrations $S \rightarrow T$ and $T \rightarrow \ast $, is a left fibration, so that $S$ is also a Kan complex. Let $A \subseteq B$ be an anodyne inclusion of simplicial sets. We must show that the map $p: S^ B \rightarrow S^ A \times _{ T^ A} T^ B$ is surjective on vertices. Since $S$ and $T$ are Kan complexes, the maps $T^ B \rightarrow T^ A$ and $S^ B \rightarrow S^ A$ are trivial fibrations. It follows that $p$ is a homotopy equivalence and a left fibration. Now we simply apply Lemma <a href="/tag/49E2DA" data-tag="49E2DA">2.1.3.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
